<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rabih az-Zubayr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1842–<a href="/years/1900">1900</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rabih az-Zubayr was a Sudanese warlord and slave trader who built a powerful state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a> region in the late nineteenth century. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a> in 1893 and threatened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a>. He was killed by French forces in 1900, but his advance was the first major external threat to reach the Wadai Empire's heartland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rabih-az-zubayr.jpg" alt="Rabih az-Zubayr" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arrantzaleak · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rabih_statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
